      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BOOM BUNNY (4) has the strongest all-round profile after a close fourth in Class 2 company at this track, beaten just over a length despite interference at the home turn. Her season has been very solid, and two wins with five placings from eleven starts at this track and distance gives her a dependable base for a BM55. LOOMING ONE (1) is the main danger dropping out of a BM65 after being steadied last start; his prior win at this venue over SPIRITOF THE OCEAN reads well and the return to 1000m suits his record. SPIRITOF THE OCEAN (7) has been runner-up at her past two, including behind Nottington Prince last time, and must be respected again as a consistent place threat with some winning chance. EXCEEDINGLY BRAZEN (6) resumes after winning a Townsville trial and has already won at this track and distance, though his fresh run has to offset a plain end to last campaign.",
